# Context

## Background
Found during an unattended end-to-end test run executed in a private
clone with CARGO_TARGET_DIR redirected. cargo xtask check failed 15
Python tests: three errors were FileNotFoundError for
target/debug/gitpickle, and the hosting suite failed with 503
"Committed generation unavailable" because the gateway tests could
not find the freshly built binary.

## Why This Way
Six tools duplicated the hardcoded relative path, so each site now
reads CARGO_TARGET_DIR with the same default. Resolving through
'cargo metadata --format-version 1' (as gitpickle_package.py does)
would also honor a config-file build.target-dir, but the repository
sets no such override, and the env lookup keeps test setup free of
extra subprocess calls.

## Gotchas
- These helpers still require the working directory to be the
  repository root; only the target directory moved.
- GITPICKLE_TEST_BINARY still takes precedence in the deployment
  tests and dist/ bundles use the release build path elsewhere.

## Verification
Reproduced the failure with CARGO_TARGET_DIR pointing at a fresh
directory: hosting 16 OK, MCP 8 OK, deployment 4 OK; MCP also
passed on the default path.
